一个轻量级 Minecraft Forge 模组，默认禁用所有粒子，仅允许用户指定的白名单粒子显示，并支持游戏内热重载配置。
🎯 主要功能
默认拦截所有粒子：进入游戏后，任何粒子效果（火焰、烟雾、爆炸等）都不会显示。
白名单机制：通过配置文件 particleinterceptor.cfg 自定义允许显示的粒子 ID（例如 minecraft:flame、minecraft:explosion）。
热重载命令：输入 /again 即可重新加载白名单，无需重启游戏。
性能优化：大幅减少不必要的粒子渲染，提升帧率，尤其适用于低配机器或大型整合包。
⚙️ 技术特点
基于 Mixin：在 ParticleManager.addEffect 方法前注入，直接取消非白名单粒子的添加，效率极高。
客户端专用：仅影响客户端渲染，服务端无需安装。
兼容 Forge 1.12.2：使用稳定映射和标准 API，兼容大多数主流模组。
📦 使用方式
将模组 JAR 放入 .minecraft/mods 文件夹。
启动游戏，模组自动生成配置文件（.minecraft/config/particleinterceptor.cfg）。
默认白名单为空，所有粒子被拦截。
编辑配置文件，按行添加粒子 ID（如 minecraft:flame）。
在游戏中输入 /again 使新配置生效。
🧪 示例配置
properties
particle {
    S:whitelist <
        minecraft:flame
        minecraft:smoke
        minecraft:explosion
     >
}
🔗 开源许可
采用 MIT License，源码托管于 GitHub，欢迎学习、修改和分发。
📌 适用场景
不喜欢大量粒子特效的玩家。
需要提升帧率、减少视觉干扰的整合包。
测试模组时临时禁用特定粒子。
一句话总结：用白名单精准控制粒子显示，让游戏更清爽、更流畅。

📝 Mod Summary: no particle (Particle Interceptor)
One-line Description
A lightweight Minecraft Forge mod that disables all particles by default, only allows user-defined whitelisted particles, and supports in‑game configuration hot‑reloading.

🎯 Main Features
All particles blocked by default: When you enter the game, no particle effects (flame, smoke, explosion, etc.) will appear.

Whitelist mechanism: Define allowed particle IDs (e.g., minecraft:flame, minecraft:explosion) in the configuration file particleinterceptor.cfg.

Hot reload command: Type /again to reload the whitelist immediately – no game restart required.

Performance boost: Significantly reduces unnecessary particle rendering, improves FPS, especially useful for low‑end machines or large modpacks.

⚙️ Technical Highlights
Mixin‑based: Injects at the beginning of ParticleManager.addEffect and cancels the addition of non‑whitelisted particles – highly efficient.

Client‑side only: Affects only client rendering; does not need to be installed on servers.

Forge 1.12.2 compatible: Uses stable mappings and standard APIs, compatible with most mainstream mods.

📦 How to Use
Place the mod JAR into your .minecraft/mods folder.

Launch the game – the mod automatically creates the configuration file (.minecraft/config/particleinterceptor.cfg).

By default the whitelist is empty, so all particles are blocked.

Edit the configuration file and add particle IDs, one per line (e.g., minecraft:flame).

In game, type /again to apply the new whitelist.

🧪 Example Configuration
properties
particle {
    S:whitelist <
        minecraft:flame
        minecraft:smoke
        minecraft:explosion
     >
}
🔗 Open Source License
Licensed under the MIT License. Source code is available on GitHub – feel free to learn, modify, and distribute.

📌 Use Cases
Players who dislike excessive particle effects.

Modpacks that aim to boost FPS and reduce visual clutter.

Temporary disabling of specific particles during mod testing.

One‑sentence summary: Precisely control which particles are shown using a whitelist – for a cleaner, smoother Minecraft experience.

